const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"用消费品的索取权理解资产",en:"Understand assets as claims on consumption goods"},body:{zh:"Lucas用一个交换经济讨论资产价格：资产提供未来产出的所有权，而消费者选择何时消费、持有什么份额。这个设定把价格与真实资源联系起来，不先假设一条股票价格路径，再把消费者行为作为事后的补充解释。",en:"Assets are ownership claims on future output in an exchange economy. Consumers choose consumption and holdings. The setup links prices to real resources rather than assuming a stock-price path first and adding consumer behavior afterward."},reference:{url:"https://www.economics.utoronto.ca/adamopou/lucas_ap.pdf",label:{zh:"1978年期刊版 · pp. 1429–1430",en:"1978 journal article · pp. 1429–1430"}}},{title:{zh:"产出过程是外生给定的",en:"Output is specified outside the pricing problem"},body:{zh:"模型的消费品不能储存，产出按给定的随机过程变化。这里没有企业根据融资成本扩张生产的完整决策。因此，研究的是既定资源流如何被定价，不能直接用来回答新增投资、技术变化或公司发行股票的全部问题。",en:"The consumption good cannot be stored, and output follows a specified stochastic process. Firms do not solve a full investment problem here. The model prices given resource flows; it does not settle questions about investment, technology or issuance."},reference:{url:"https://www.economics.utoronto.ca/adamopou/lucas_ap.pdf",label:{zh:"1978年期刊版 · p. 1430",en:"1978 journal article · p. 1430"}}},{title:{zh:"分红与交易的先后影响价格含义",en:"Dividend timing changes what a price means"},body:{zh:"当期产出先分配给原有持有人，随后交易的份额对应未来所有权。由此得到的价格是与这一时间顺序一致的价格。阅读收益公式时，必须确认分红是否已经支付；把含息与除息价格混用，会改变所计算的资产收益。",en:"Current output goes to existing owners before shares are traded. Prices must be interpreted using that sequence. A return calculation needs to know whether the dividend has already been paid; mixing cum-dividend and ex-dividend prices changes the object measured."},reference:{url:"https://www.economics.utoronto.ca/adamopou/lucas_ap.pdf",label:{zh:"1978年期刊版 · p. 1430",en:"1978 journal article · p. 1430"}}},{title:{zh:"理性预期是一致性条件",en:"Rational expectations impose consistency"},body:{zh:"消费者根据预期价格作决定，所有人的决定又通过市场出清形成价格。论文要求这两种价格描述相互一致。这个条件并不等于解释投资者如何学习，也不能被简单翻译成每个人都能准确预测下一次实现的价格。",en:"Consumers choose using expected price behavior, while market clearing generates prices from those choices. Rational expectations require consistency between the two descriptions. They neither explain learning nor imply accurate prediction of each realized future price."},reference:{url:"https://www.economics.utoronto.ca/adamopou/lucas_ap.pdf",label:{zh:"1978年期刊版 · p. 1431",en:"1978 journal article · p. 1431"}}},{title:{zh:"没有交易量仍可能有资产价格",en:"Prices can exist without equilibrium trade"},body:{zh:"同质消费者在均衡中持有既定份额，并消费全部当期产出，因此不需要持续交换资产。价格仍然有意义，因为它支持每个人不愿偏离的选择。这个模型适合讨论定价一致性，却不能据此解释真实市场频繁交易的原因。",en:"Identical consumers hold the equilibrium shares and consume current output, so continuing asset exchange is unnecessary. Prices still support choices that nobody wishes to change. This is useful for pricing consistency but not an explanation of active real-world trading."},reference:{url:"https://www.economics.utoronto.ca/adamopou/lucas_ap.pdf",label:{zh:"1978年期刊版 · pp. 1430–1432",en:"1978 journal article · pp. 1430–1432"}}},{title:{zh:"最优选择与市场出清缺一不可",en:"Optimal choice and market clearing are both required"},body:{zh:"均衡定义同时要求给定价格下的消费与持仓最优，以及这些选择与资源和份额供给相容。只解消费者问题还没有完成整个定价问题，反过来仅找到供需相等的价格，也不能省略偏好与预算约束带来的行为条件。",en:"Equilibrium requires optimal consumption and holdings at given prices, plus compatibility with resource and share supply. Solving the consumer problem alone is incomplete; a market-clearing price also needs behavior consistent with preferences and budget constraints."},reference:{url:"https://www.economics.utoronto.ca/adamopou/lucas_ap.pdf",label:{zh:"1978年期刊版 · p. 1432 · definition",en:"1978 journal article · p. 1432 · definition"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"模型中的同质消费者、外生产出和无储存消费品是刻意简化。它研究价格如何与决策相容，不是对现实交易量或投资者学习过程的直接解释。",en:"Identical consumers, exogenous output and a perishable consumption good are deliberate simplifications. The model studies consistency between prices and choices, not actual trading volume or learning."}};export{e as default};
